# Everything goes through a gateway. Both the public and admin gateways now route /api/demo/* to this
# service (cluster "service-api"), validating the token and forwarding the actor headers.
@gateway = https://localhost:7225
# Admin gateway alternative: https://localhost:7226
@serviceDirect = https://localhost:7300

### 1) Get an access token (through the gateway's /connect route). Copy access_token into @token below.
POST {{gateway}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&username=admin&password=Admin123!&client_id=11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111&client_secret=secret

### Paste the access_token from the response:
@token = PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### 2) Public — no token required (anonymous route at the edge).
GET {{gateway}}/api/demo/public

### 3) Token only — any valid token (401 at the gateway without one).
GET {{gateway}}/api/demo/token
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4) Who am I — the actor the gateway forwarded (X-User-Id / X-Client-Id).
GET {{gateway}}/api/demo/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5) Permission (user/RBAC dimension) — needs the 'demo.read' permission.
#    To make it pass: on the provider, create permission 'demo.read', grant it to a role,
#    and assign that role to your user. 403 until then.
GET {{gateway}}/api/demo/permission
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6) Scope (client dimension) — needs a scope covering 'manage:identity'.
#    The seeded client (identity.manage) passes out of the box.
GET {{gateway}}/api/demo/scope
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7) Both dimensions together.
GET {{gateway}}/api/demo/permission-and-scope
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### (Optional) Same call straight to the service, bypassing the gateway.
GET {{serviceDirect}}/api/demo/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
